    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I don't know if there's even a tale left to tell. What's the point of recounting the details when the outcome is so final? The men... they looked to me for a future, and all I gave them was a grave. I look at my hands and I don't see a commander anymore. I just see a man who doesn't deserve to see the sunrise. I feel like I'm just waiting for something to make it right. To balance the scales.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
